# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ — the ETL. See the root .gitignore for secrets, __pycache__ and OS junk.
# What follows is only what this folder generates.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Regenerable and per-machine. In CI these are restored with actions/cache
# instead of being committed, so the repo does not grow twice a day.
# A cache miss is harmless: API-Football's own reported usage re-syncs the
# daily counter on the next run, and that is the authoritative number anyway.
# (33 MB locally at the time of writing — this is the rule that matters most.)
output/cache/
output/.quota.json

# Legacy Mode A output (collectors/ + run.py). pipeline.py supersedes it and
# writes model_data.csv instead; training.csv is a rebuildable leftover.
output/training.csv

# Half-written files if a run is interrupted mid-flush.
output/*.tmp
output/*.partial

# --- deliberately NOT ignored, so do not "tidy" these away -----------------
# output/model_data.csv   the training set. Committed once and refreshed by
#                         hand before a retrain (workflow_dispatch ->
#                         refresh-dataset commits it).
# output/.manifest.json   which sources produced the rows above.
# output/fixtures.csv     the last --live snapshot; small, and useful as a
#                         reference of the exact column shape.
# output/conflicts.csv    the data-quality report the workflow commits.
# unsorted/               16 MB of raw season CSVs. They are the *input* to
#                         `pipeline.py --with-api`, so refresh-dataset in CI
#                         cannot rebuild the dataset without them.
